"note_claim": "Romans built thousands of public bathhouses across Europe centuries before the Moors arrived in Iberia in 711 AD",
"label": "SUPPORTS",
"quote": "Baths sprang up all over the empire. Where natural hot springs existed (as in Bath, England ; Băile Herculane , Romania or Aquae Calidae near Burgas and Serdica , Bulgaria ) thermae were built around them.",
"reason": "The page confirms Ancient Romans built public bathhouses across their empire, including European locations like England and Romania, during antiquity (e.g., 216 AD)."
